# What shellcheck leaves alone in Hyprdori's scripts (hyprdori-check runs it): ways of writing
# that are meant, not mistakes.
#   SC1007  a= b= on one line sets both empty
#   SC1010  "done" as an argument (hyprdori-present done)
#   SC2001  sed where ${var//a/b} would do
#   SC2012  ls to list a folder's files by time
#   SC2013  a for loop over grep's words
#   SC2015  a && b || c, where b doesn't fail
#   SC2016  $ kept as it is inside single quotes (awk, sed, bash -c)
#   SC2017  division before multiplication, to round down to a whole cell
#   SC2054  commas inside one array element (kernel options)
#   SC2100  a word with a dash in it after = isn't arithmetic
#   SC2174  mkdir -p -m for the last folder only
#   SC2206  numbers from $(( )) unquoted in an array
disable=SC1007,SC1010,SC2001,SC2012,SC2013,SC2015,SC2016,SC2017,SC2054,SC2100,SC2174,SC2206
